KZ2 patch 6069: LD_REC_MEMO, the recording memo. Default off. Plus a fix of patch 2045's state
memo: ld_downsample and ld_scaled_blit now invalidate it.

From the Killzone 3 port's walker plan (Project Helghast docs/in-progress/walker-plan.md step 2 and section 5 item 2; plan
only, no KZ3 patch; the Killzone 3 PC port "Project Helghast", same author, MIT); written here.
Patch 2045's per-list state memo (g_ld_sm) skips SetPipelineState, SetGraphicsRootSignature, SetDescriptorHeaps and
OMSetRenderTargets when unchanged; every draw still recorded RSSetViewports, RSSetScissorRects, the stencil reference
(OMSetStencilRef or the per-face call), OMSetBlendFactor, OMSetDepthBounds, IASetVertexBuffers, IASetPrimitiveTopology
(always TRIANGLELIST), up to three SetGraphicsRootDescriptorTable and two SetGraphicsRootConstantBufferView. With
LD_REC_MEMO=1 (or T: KZ2_WALKER_TOGGLE's phase, patch 6067) each is skipped when it equals the value last recorded on
the same command list in the same state-memo generation (g_ld_sm_gen: list Reset and every path that binds its own
pipeline, root signature or heaps); the root arguments are also forgotten whenever the root signature is set. The memo
is live only while the state memo is (LD_NO_STATE_MEMO=1 turns both off). With RSX_PERF=1 [perf-walk2] ends with
"| rec-memo skips N" (calls skipped in the period).
The fix (always on): ld_downsample and ld_scaled_blit (NV3089 scaled resolves done as draws) set their own PSO, root
signature, heaps and render target on the live list without LD_SM_INVALIDATE, so a following draw with the PSO the
memo remembered skipped SetPipelineState and drew with the blit's pipeline. KZ2's heavy view has no NV3089 blits
([perf-nv3089] n=0), so nothing seen changes there. Both functions are upstream ps3recomp v0.18.0 code and 2045 is
KZ3's patch, so ASSUMPTION: KZ3 has the same gap (not checked in KZ3's tree).

